INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<p>One of the most important questions farmers face, especially during the autumn and spring planting seasons, is <strong>the required onion seed rate per hectare.</strong> Determining this amount is not just a fixed number; it depends on many variables, including onion variety, seed vigor, seed quality, soil moisture, and the irrigation system. Onion is one of the most popular fresh vegetables used as a primary flavoring agent in many dishes. The goal of this guide is to provide a comprehensive and practical perspective for calculating optimal seed usage and coordinating it with drip and tape irrigation systems, to conserve water resources and increase crop yield.</p><h2>Factors determining onion seed rate per hectare</h2><p>Before any calculation, you must understand that the final onion yield is directly related to planting density and seed quality. Old or weak seeds always require higher consumption. Below are the most important influencing factors:</p><ul><li><strong>Seed quality and vigor:</strong> Seeds with vigor above 95% require a lower quantity compared to weak seeds. Always review the seed lab report before purchasing.</li><li><strong>Onion variety type:</strong> Local varieties exhibit different seed consumption rates and ground coverage behaviors compared to improved varieties.</li><li><strong>Cultivation objective:</strong> If the objective is harvesting green shoots, the seeding density differs from that required when the goal is producing large bulbs.</li></ul><p>It is generally recommended to use between 15 and 25 kilograms of seed per hectare for conventional onion seedling cultivation, although this figure may vary depending on environmental conditions. To better understand the importance of controlling seeding density for other crops, you can refer to [Topic: Calculating Tritical Seed Rate per Hectare](https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%AA%D8%B1%DB%8C%DB%8C%D8%AA%DB%8C%DA%A9%D8%A7%D9%84%DA%AF%D9%87-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/) on our site, which explains similar principles.</p><h2>Impact of drip and tape irrigation systems on yield</h2><p>One of the major challenges in onion seedling cultivation is managing water delivery to its small and sensitive roots. In dry conditions, excessive spraying can cause surface soil erosion and stress the plant. In contrast, drip and tape irrigation systems allow for precise water delivery to the root zone. When you <strong>onion seed rate per hectare</strong> adjust based on your designed irrigation system, you can maximize yield.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-پیازچه-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقدار بذر پیازچه در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>seed rate per hectare Onion Set</figcaption></figure><h3>optimal drip line spacing for Onion Set cultivation</h3><p>Drip line spacing must be adjusted based on planting density. If using a lower seed rate, it may be necessary to reduce drip line spacing to ensure water coverage in empty areas. Conversely, using drip tape for sensitive vegetables like Onion Set is very common, as it creates a gentler water flow. If you are having trouble installing your equipment or are looking for technical guidance, the article on [How to Install Drip Irrigation Tape](https://navar-abyari.ir/tarzi-nasbi-lulayi-ob-yori-tip/) can serve as a good guide.</p><h2>Precise calculation and practical sowing tips</h2><p>For quality Onion Set sowing, adherence to standard cultivation protocols is essential. Sowing too deeply can delay germination, as Onion Set is a shallow-rooted plant. Below are the practical steps for sowing and seed management:</p><ol><li><strong>Seedbed preparation:</strong> Soil must be prepared for vegetable cultivation by addressing chemical pesticide concentrations, salinity, and texture.</li><li><strong>Sowing Onion Set:</strong> Sow the seeds at a depth of 1 to 2 cm and cover them with appropriate soil.</li><li><strong>Start of irrigation:</strong> The first irrigation after sowing must be applied with low pressure and care to prevent seed washing.</li><li><strong>Growth monitoring:</strong> If seedling density is lower than expected, gap-fill seeds into bare spots.</li></ol><p>Also, to compare yield with other crops, reading [Oat yield per hectare guide](https://navar-abyari.ir/oat-yield-per-hectare-guide/) may be helpful, as water management principles for cereals and vegetables share similar overlaps. Precise seedling management is the foundation for a sustainable and water-stress-free crop.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-پیازچه-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر پیازچه در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>seed rate per hectare crop spring wheat</figcaption></figure><h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2><h3>1. What is the best time for planting green onions per hectare?</h3><p>The best planting time depends on the geographic region and climate. In cold regions, autumn planting usually requires less seed because the plants have more time to grow and establish. In warm regions, spring and summer planting (using shade netting) are more common.</p><h3>2. Can drip tape be used for green onions?</h3><p>Yes, drip tape is one of the best options for green onions because it increases moisture around the plants and reduces surface evaporation. However, ensure that the output of the tape does not cause waterlogging around the stem, which can lead to fungal diseases. To correctly adjust water pressure in these systems, it is recommended to study [Drip Tape Water Pressure Measurement Guide](https://navar-abyari.ir/measuring-drip-tape-water-pressure-iq/).</p><h3>3. What should you do if green onion seed quality is poor?</h3><p>If you do not have seed backing, always increase the seed application rate by 20 to 30 percent. You can also complete ground coverage by making repeated plantings in empty areas. Precise seed management means always working with high-quality seed at the right time.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-پیازچه-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر پیازچه در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>seed rate per hectare crop green onions</figcaption></figure><h3>4. What is the appropriate planting distance for green onions?</h3><p>Row spacing is typically 20 to 30 cm, and in-row spacing is 5 to 10 cm. These dimensions help you calculate the required seed quantity more accurately.</p><h2>Conclusion: Coordination of Seed, Water, and Yield</h2><p>Success in onion scallion cultivation and, consequently, achieving profitability requires precise coordination between <strong>Onion scallion seed rate per hectare</strong> and irrigation systems. Using drip and tape systems not only saves water but also creates a stable growing environment, allowing plants to maximize their use of soil nutrients. A smart farmer adjusts the seed based on seed quality and soil conditions and then modifies the irrigation system according to this density. By following the mentioned points and using practical resources, you can deliver more uniform and higher-quality produce to the market.</p>\n<p><strong>Related Articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/hosilnokiya-chukandari-qand-dar-gektar-omilhoi-muassisir/">hosilnokiya chukandari qand dar gektar omilhoi muassisir</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/oat-yield-per-hectare-guide/">oat yield per hectare guide</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/corn-drip-tape-spacing-forage-corn-guide/">corn drip tape spacing forage corn guide</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%AA%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%DB%8C%DA%A9%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%87-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">D985D982D8AFD8A7D8B1 D8A8D8B0D8B1 D8AAD8B1DB8CD8AADB8CDAA9D8A7D984D987 D8AFD8B1 D987DAA9D8AAD8A7D8B1</a></p>','Onion Seed Rate per Hectare: A Comprehensive Guide to Cultivation, Drip, and Subsurface Drip Irrigation','For successful small onion cultivation, accurately determining the seeding rate per hectare is critical. This guide examines the principles of optimal planting density, its impact on yield, and water resource management using modern irrigation systems.','publish','closed','closed','onion-seed-rate-hectare-comprehensive-cultivation-drip-sdi-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
